    "description": "**Summary**\n\nDeal\\__c already has the logic a \\`region\\` field needs — it's just embedded separately inside the Deal Name and External Deal ID before-save flows instead of living on a reusable field. Add a new formula field, Region_Codec, that surfaces that value directly, matching the CMS webhook's own region format: US state deals get a US- prefix (US-NJ), Canadian province deals don't (AB), and country-wide deals resolve to US/CA. Reuses Market_State_Code_\\_c's existing state CASE logic rather than adding a third copy of the 64-value list.\n\n**Proposed solution**\n\n1\\. Add formula field Region_Code\\__c (Text) on Deal_\\_c:\n\nIF(\n\nISPICKVAL(Market_State__c, \"\"),\n\nCASE(TEXT(Market_Country__c),\n\n\"United States\", \"US\",\n\n\"Canada\", \"CA\",\n\n\"\"),\n\nIF(\n\nTEXT(Market_Country__c) = \"United States\",\n\n\"US-\" & Market_State_Code__c,\n\nMarket_State_Code__c\n\n)\n\n)\n\n2\\. No page layout placement — automation/reporting field only, same pattern as Market_State_Code\\__c, Market_Country_Codec, Source_Code_\\_c (BUILD-246).\n\nField Description (ready to paste):\n\n\"Region code for the deal's market — for a US state-specific deal, US- + the 2-letter state code (e.g. US-NJ); for a Canadian province-specific deal, the bare province code (e.g. AB, no country prefix); otherwise US/CA for a country-wide deal.\"\n\nHelp Text: n/a — not on page layouts.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n1\\. Market_Country\\__c = United States, Market_Statec = New Jersey → Region_Code_\\_c = \"US-NJ\".\n\n2\\. Market_Country\\__c = Canada, Market_Statec = Alberta → Region_Code_\\_c = \"AB\" (no CA- prefix).\n\n3\\. Market_Country\\__c = United States, Market_Statec blank → Region_Code_\\_c = \"US\".\n\n4\\. Market_Country\\__c = Canada, Market_Statec blank → Region_Code_\\_c = \"CA\".\n\n5\\. Both blank → Region_Code__c = \"\" (blank, not an error).",
